languageModelTools.modelDescription:
Changes the structure of a table/matrix (Tablix) – error-prone in XML because TablixColumns, TablixRows, cells, the row/column hierarchies and spans must stay consistent. Operations (run in order; row and column numbers are 0-based as listed by bcReport_inspectLayout and refer to the table as left by the previous operation):
- insertColumn {at?, width?, field?, values?}: new column at index (default: end); `field` fills header caption and detail =Fields!<field>.Value with BC formats; `values` per row index
- deleteColumn {at}; setColumnWidth {at, width}
- insertRow {row, place: above|below|outsideAbove|outsideBelow, values?}: outside* = outside the innermost group of that row
- deleteRow {row}; setRowHeight {row, height}
- headerRow / footerRow {present}: table header/footer row outside all groups
- addGroup {row, mode: parent|child, expression, name?, header?, footer?}: row group around the group of `row` (parent) or inside it around the details (child), with group header (default) / footer rows
- deleteGroup {group, deleteRows?}; addGroupRow {group, which: header|footer}
- setGroup {group, expressions?, sort?: [{value, descending?}], filters?: [{expression, operator?, values}], pageBreak?: ""|Start|End|StartAndEnd|Between, hidden?}
- addColumnGroup {column, expression, name?}; deleteColumnGroup {group, deleteColumns?}
- mergeCells {cells: [names]} (adjacent cells of one row); splitCell {cell}
- setCell {row, column, value?, style?}
- setDataSet {dataSet}
Returns the new structure. A Tablix not marked "editable with bcReport_editTable" in the overview must be edited in the XML.
